---
import Section from './Section.astro';

const rows = [
  { tool: 'Claude Code', store: 'JSONL files in its own folder', catch: 'Deleted after 30 days by default.' },
  { tool: 'Codex', store: 'Rollout files, compressed', catch: 'Its own layout and compression.' },
  { tool: 'Cursor', store: 'One SQLite database', catch: 'No bulk export.' },
  { tool: 'ChatGPT', store: 'On a server', catch: 'A ZIP file, by request, by hand.' },
  { tool: 'Claude.ai', store: 'On a server', catch: 'A ZIP file, by request. The link expires after 24 hours.' },
];
---

<Section
  id="why"
  eyebrow="The problem"
  title="A session lives in one tool, on one machine. Until it is deleted."
>
  <div class="border-b border-line">
    <div class="hidden grid-cols-[1fr_1.4fr_1.8fr] gap-6 pb-3 font-mono text-[12.5px] text-muted md:grid">
      <span>Tool</span>
      <span>Keeps your sessions as</span>
      <span>The catch</span>
    </div>
    {
      rows.map((row) => (
        <div class="grid gap-1 border-t border-line py-4 md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.4fr_1.8fr] md:gap-6">
          <span class="font-medium">{row.tool}</span>
          <span class="text-muted">{row.store}</span>
          <span>{row.catch}</span>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <p class="mt-10 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Five tools, five formats. Moving between them means starting over, or importing a trimmed copy.{' '}
    <span class="text-ink">OCF puts one format in the middle.</span>
  </p>
</Section>
